.TH QADAM-FLOW-MINT-WORKER-TOKEN 1 "October 2026" "Qadam Flow" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
qadam-flow-mint-worker-token \- derive a worker token from the master's JWT secret
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qadam-flow-mint-worker-token
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qadam-flow-mint-worker-token
runs on the host that holds the
.B qadam-flow
master — the host carrying
.BR /etc/qadam-flow/master.conf —
and prints the
.B AP_WORKER_TOKEN
that a distributed worker uses to authenticate against it. The token is an
HS256 JWT signed with the master's
.B AP_JWT_SECRET
(read locally, passed to the signer through the environment and never
printed); the signing parameters are the same as the Docker image's
\fIdocker-entrypoint.sh\fR mints: 100-year expiry, keyid 1, issuer
.BR qadam-flow ,
token type WORKER.
.PP
Paste the printed token as
.B AP_WORKER_TOKEN
in the worker host's
.B /etc/qadam-flow/worker.conf
(permissions stay 0600) and restart the worker. The master's serializer
secrets never leave their host: only the derived token travels.
.PP
The command takes no arguments and provides no overrides; both the config
paths and the signing parameters are fixed, so every host using the same
master mints compatible tokens.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /etc/qadam-flow/master.conf
Read locally to obtain the signing secret; never printed.
.TP
.B /etc/qadam-flow/worker.conf
On the WORKER host only: receives the printed token as
.BR AP_WORKER_TOKEN .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The token was printed to stdout.
.TP
.B 1
Fatal: the master config is unreadable, has no
.B AP_JWT_SECRET\fR, or
.B /usr/lib/qadam-flow
(the signing node_modules) is not installed. The reason is printed to stderr.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR qadam-flow-worker (1),
.BR qadam-flow-master (1),
.BR systemctl (1)
.PP
Full distributed-install walkthrough (REDIS+Postgres layout, two hosts):
.B /usr/share/doc/qadam-flow-common/README.Debian
